## Question 4: Display the Top 3 Influencers Per Platform

### Sample Table: Influencers

| id | platform | followers |
|---:|---|---:|
| 1 | Instagram | 900000 |
| 2 | Instagram | 750000 |
| 3 | Instagram | 600000 |
| 4 | Instagram | 500000 |
| 5 | YouTube | 1200000 |
| 6 | YouTube | 950000 |
| 7 | YouTube | 800000 |
| 8 | YouTube | 650000 |
| 9 | TikTok | 700000 |
| 10 | TikTok | 550000 |
| 11 | TikTok | 400000 |
| 12 | TikTok | 300000 |

### SQL Query

```sql
WITH RankedInfluencers AS (
    SELECT
        id,
        platform,
        followers,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
            PARTITION BY platform
            ORDER BY followers DESC, id ASC
        ) AS row_num
    FROM Influencers
)
SELECT
    id,
    platform,
    followers,
    row_num
FROM RankedInfluencers
WHERE row_num <= 3
ORDER BY platform, row_num;
```

### Result Output

| id | platform | followers | row_num |
|---:|---|---:|---:|
| 1 | Instagram | 900000 | 1 |
| 2 | Instagram | 750000 | 2 |
| 3 | Instagram | 600000 | 3 |
| 9 | TikTok | 700000 | 1 |
| 10 | TikTok | 550000 | 2 |
| 11 | TikTok | 400000 | 3 |
| 5 | YouTube | 1200000 | 1 |
| 6 | YouTube | 950000 | 2 |
| 7 | YouTube | 800000 | 3 |

**Explanation:** The CTE `RankedInfluencers` assigns a row number to influencers separately within each platform. The main query filters the result to include only rows numbered 1, 2, and 3, giving the top three influencers per platform. The `id` column breaks ties in follower counts.

